      "id": "claim_7cc4d7fe277b4b2897513a2a035b65b0",
      "statement": "Permission enforcement distinguishes exact-path tools (read_file, write_file, edit_file) that fire on their single path from bulk tools (ls, glob, grep, delete) that fire when their search subtree could overlap an anchored rule prefix, and a pathless bulk call such as grep(path=None) fires unconditionally for any interrupt-mode rule.",
